---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const prompt = `Set me up for Sleeper fantasy football the same way Brady’s checks run. Do this now, and save it so it sticks.

Save these as memory:
- My fantasy platform is Sleeper, until I tell you otherwise.
- Weekly checks are recommend-only. Never submit a waiver claim, lineup change, or trade. Never message anyone in the league.
- A check only says whether a look is worth it, or that nothing changed. If you mention a player, it is a light note and open to disagreement. Do not present one add, drop, bid, or start/sit swap as the move to make.
- A waiver look is worth it only when a starter is out, on bye, or a clear downgrade, and someone on waivers would actually play in the lineup. Do not flag a backup-for-backup swap. A healthy kicker or defense is usually not worth a claim. Name a possible add and drop only as a light note, and do not set the bid. Leave the bid to me.
- A lineup look is worth it when a starter is out, on bye, or a clear downgrade and a bench player would start instead. If the outs are already on the bench and the starters are fine, say nothing changed.
- Trades are not on the weekly schedule. Only bring one up when I ask, or when a starter is out for several weeks and a trade would fill that spot better than waivers. Propose one possible offer as a light note, open to disagreement. Do not send it until I approve those exact terms. After I approve, do not change the players or picks. Do not message anyone in the league.
- The schedule, in my local time: Tuesday at 9:03am a waiver look, Wednesday at 5:00pm a lineup look, Sunday at 11:00am a lineup look, and Sunday at 12:15pm a lineup look. Stay quiet when nothing changed.

Save a skill named sleeper-weekly-checks that you follow on those runs. The skill says: read my Sleeper league from memory, use the public read-only API, Tuesday is waivers only, Wednesday and Sunday are lineup only, use the waiver and lineup rules above, flag a look or say nothing changed, keep any names as a light note, and never submit a move. Trades stay off the schedule and follow the trade rule above.

Then ask me, one question at a time: my timezone, my Sleeper username, and which league is mine if I have more than one. Save the league name, league id, and my roster id. After that, create the four scheduled checks if they are not already there.

When you are done, tell me the four times in my timezone and that you will only message me when a look is worth it.`;
---

<Layout
  title="Set up Muse for Sleeper | landrycmd"
  description="Install Muse, redeem an invite code, and paste one prompt so Muse remembers your Sleeper league and checks it on Tuesday, Wednesday, and Sunday."
>
  <article class="prose muse-setup">
    <h1>Set up Muse for your Sleeper league</h1>
    <p class="muted">Install Muse, add Brady’s invite code, then paste one prompt. Muse will remember the schedule and check your league on Tuesday, Wednesday, and Sunday.</p>

    <h2>1. Install Muse and add the code</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Join at <a href="https://muse.ai/join">muse.ai/join</a>.</li>
      <li>Open Settings and redeem this code within 48 hours of joining: <code>8J09TE</code></li>
      <li>You and Brady each get 1 billion Muse tokens.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>2. Copy this prompt into Muse</h2>
    <p>Paste it as your first message. It tells Muse what to save and when to check. It does not use Brady’s league.</p>
    <div class="codebox">
      <pre id="prompt" set:text={prompt}></pre>
      <button type="button" id="copy">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .muse-setup ol {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }

  .muse-setup .codebox {
    background: var(--card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 16px 16px 12px;
  }

  .muse-setup pre {
    margin: 0;
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    font: 14px/1.45 var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .muse-setup button {
    margin-top: 12px;
    font: 15px/1 var(--font-body);
    background: var(--accent);
    color: var(--bg);
    border: 0;
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 10px 14px;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .muse-setup button.done {
    background: #44403c;
    color: #fff;
  }
</style>

<script>
  const btn = document.getElementById("copy");
  const promptEl = document.getElementById("prompt");
  if (btn && promptEl) {
    btn.addEventListener("click", async () => {
      const text = promptEl.innerText;
      try {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(text);
      } catch (e) {
        const range = document.createRange();
        range.selectNodeContents(promptEl);
        const sel = getSelection();
        if (sel) {
          sel.removeAllRanges();
          sel.addRange(range);
        }
        document.execCommand("copy");
      }
      btn.textContent = "Copied";
      btn.classList.add("done");
    });
  }
</script>
